        "message": "Add opt-in GPU rendering for the hotel fixture\n\nThe thread-probe diagnostic showed the RGB-D camera's llvmpipe software\nrendering saturating the console Gazebo server (~3 cores continuously,\nmain thread ~80%) and stalling physics beyond the 100 ms command budget\non non-GPU nodes. A new --gpu-rendering runner flag pins the fixture to\na GPU worker, requests one nvidia.com/gpu with full driver capabilities\n(feasibility-verified: libEGL_nvidia and the graphics stack are mounted),\ntolerates the g5/g6e taints, and sets PHASE5_HEADLESS_RENDERING=1; the\nconsole server then selects EGL headless rendering via ServerConfig.\nThe forced-software GL profile is unchanged for non-GPU runs. The flag\nrequires a pinned node, hotel suite, and is mutually exclusive with the\nnon-GPU placement guards; the summary records headless_gpu_rendering.\nRendering-context selection only: physics, watchdog, and every safety\nthreshold are unchanged."
      },
      "type": "Git"
    },
